+\paragraph{Restricted native P2 accepted FE strain option.}
+The explicitly selected \texttt{Bulk history representation = accepted FE strain}
+is a separate default-off total-energy verification model. The authoritative
+bulk internal state is an FE vector $d_R$, with
+$\boldsymbol R=\operatorname{symgrad}d_R=\boldsymbol E^{\rm tot}-\boldsymbol E^{\rm in}$.
+It is not a projection of particle stress or an accumulated total displacement.
+For identical homogeneous bulk/fault $G,\eta$, let
+\[
+ \beta=\exp(-\Delta t G/\eta),\quad
+ \kappa=\eta(1-\beta),\quad
+ d_R^{n+1}=\beta d_R^n+(\kappa/G)\boldsymbol u^{n+1}.
+\]
+At a phase trial, hold accepted $d_R^n,Z^n$ fixed and reconstruct
+$\boldsymbol\tau(\phi)=2G[\operatorname{symgrad}d_R^n-(Z^n/G)\chi(\phi)\mathcal S]$.
+The same state supplies mechanical history and bulk energy
+$\sum_a JxW_a\boldsymbol\tau_a:\boldsymbol\tau_a/(4G)$.
+The phase functional also contains $\sum_b ds_b Z_b^2/(2G I_b)$ and the native
+CPDI fracture functional, including the exact consistent-normalization adjoint;
+$\mathcal H^+$ is diagnostic rather than a phase driver in this option.
+Initial relaxation retains the existing native seeded-H procedure. The accepted
+seed is then protected by the previous-phase lower bound, with unloaded $d_R=Z=0$.
+Endpoint mechanics follows instantaneous elastic profile redistribution.
+Prepare and validate the complete step before publishing $d_R,Z$, derived
+particle samples and diagnostic H. Phase and mechanical trials never change
+accepted $d_R$. Particle samples are not reprojected into this mechanical history.
+
+The phase assembly differentiates in independent nodal $(\phi,I)$ coordinates
+and pulls back through $D I=P D b$ once. Its full Hessian contains the second
+normalization derivative as well as the cross terms. A positive Gauss--Newton
+search metric may replace negative free-set curvature, with a projected-gradient
+line-search safeguard. Primal-dual contact prediction uses the positive diagonal
+metric, including the nonzero increment to a predicted bound and its symmetric
+column lift; the residual, energy, constraints and KKT tolerances
+remain those of the same functional. The arithmetic allowance uses the positive
+pre-cancellation term scale, including the normalization adjoint. It is an
+uncertainty estimate, not phase viscosity or a physical regularization.
+
+This initial option requires serial 2-D uniform Cartesian Box cells, one fixed
+horizontal through-going fault with full normal association, homogeneous identical
+bulk/fault coefficients ($\lambda=\eta/G$, 100 s in the reference fixture), AT1
+and Lorentz $p=1$, consistent normalization, surface elastic-slip history,
+bulk-conjugate endpoint mechanics, direct phase irreversibility, and unloaded
+initialization. Mesh/geometry changes, history transport, particle replenishment,
+external retained-stress overrides and coefficient variation are rejected.
+The initial implementation is fresh-run only: resume is rejected, including
+particle-stress checkpoints; a registry marker also forbids resuming this option's
+checkpoint through the particle-authoritative path. No implicit conversion is
+defined. Existing defaults and the particle-authoritative path are unchanged.
 
